        {
          "page": 2,
          "text": "UNCLASSIFIED U.S. Department of State Case No. M-2017-11755 Doc No. C06550458 Date: 05/31/2018\n\n                                      M-2017-11755    B-00001350811      \"UNCLASSIFIED\"       7/10/2026\n\n\n\n\n      NATO INTERNATIONAL STAFF:\n      SECRETARY GENERAL JAVIER SOLANA (SPAIN)\n      DEPUTY SECRETARY GENERAL SERGIG BALANZINO (ITALY)\n       PRIVATE OFFICE DIRECTOR JORGE DOMECQ (SPAIN)\n       PRIVATE OFFICE DEPUTY DIRECTOR HOYT YEE (U.S.).\n\n         4. (C) SUMMARY. THE SECRETARY MET WITH NATO SECRETARY\n      GENERAL SOLANA BEFORE THE NAC MINISTERIAL PLENARY SESSION\n      DECEMBER 8 TO REVIEW MINISTERIAL AND SUMMIT ISSUES/                                                                           25X6\n                                                                           25X9\n\n                 CONFIDENTIAL\n\n      PAGE 03   STATE 230684 152118Z\n                                                                           25X6\n                                                                           25X9\n\n\n\n                                THE SECRETARY AND SOLANA\n      AGREED THAT THIS MINISTERIAL SESSION WAS PREPARATORY TO THE\n     WORK TO BE COMPLETED -- AND DECISIONS TO BE TAKEN -- AT THE\n      WASHINGTON SUMMIT IN APRIL. THE SECRETARY WAS EAGER TO\n      HEAR WHAT ALLIES HAD TO SAY ON ALL THESE ISSUES. END\n      SUMMARY.\n\n       FIRST WARNING ON \"NO FIRST USE\"\n\n                                                                           25X6\n                                                                           25X9\n\n\n\n\n\n      STRATEGIC CONCEPT AND OPEN DOOR ISSUES\n\n                                                                            25X6\n                                                                            25X9\n\n\n\n\n\nUNCLASSIFIED U.S. Department of State Case No. M-2017-11755 Doc No. C06550458 Date: 05/31/2018"
        },
        {
          "page": 3,
          "text": "UNCLASSIFIED U.S. Department of State Case No. M-2017-11755 Doc No. C06550458 Date: 05/31/2018\n\n                                      M-2017-11755    B-00001350811      \"UNCLASSIFIED\"       7/10/2026\n\n\n\n                                                                           25X6\n                                                                           25X9\n\n\n\n\n\n       ALLIES CAUTION ON WMD INITIATIVE: UN MANDATE ISSUE\n\n                                                                            25X6\n                                                                            25X9\n\n\n\n\n\n      THE SECRETARY RESPONDS\n\n          8. (C) THE SECRETARY AGREED THERE WOULD BE NO MAJOR\n       DECISIONS TAKEN AT THIS MINISTERIAL. BUT THE ALLIANCE IS\n     ON A GOOD PATH TOWARD WASHINGTON. WE NEED TO GET THE\n      STRATEGIC CONCEPT RIGHT, AND RESOLVE THE FUNDAMENTAL ISSUES\n      AS SOON AS POSSIBLE. THERE ARE, HOWEVER, SOME PROBLEMS\n      THAT WE CANNOT AVOID. THE MANDATE ISSUE, FOR EXAMPLE, IS\n\n      AN IRRITATING ON THAT WILL CONTINUE TO BE RAISED.\n       ASSISTANT SECRETARY GROSSMAN NOTED THAT THE MANDATE ISSUE\n      HAD A PARTICULAR INTEREST FOR THE U.S. SENATE. THE\n      SECRETARY ADDED THAT BECAUSE THE ISSUE WAS UNAVOIDABLE, WE\n     WOULD TRY NOT TO BE TOO PROVOCATIVE. SHE ADDED THAT A\n       PRECISE, NON-TECHNICAL VISION STATEMENT FOR NATO IS AN\n      IMPORTANT GOAL FOR THE SUMMIT.\n\n          9. (C) THE SECRETARY SAID THAT SOLANA'S OPEN DOOR\n      DISCUSSIONS WITH ALLIES WERE WELCOMED, AND SHE HOPED THAT\n      CONSENSUS COULD SOON BE REACHED TO CLEARLY DEMONSTRATE OUR\n      COMMITMENT TO THE ENLARGEMENT PROCESS, WHICH IS CENTRAL TO\n     OUR STRATEGIC VISION. WE WOULD NEED TO SEE HOW THE\n                 CONFIDENTIAL\n\n\n\n\nUNCLASSIFIED U.S. Department of State Case No. M-2017-11755 Doc No. C06550458 Date: 05/31/2018"
        },
        {
          "page": 4,
          "text": "UNCLASSIFIED U.S. Department of State Case No. M-2017-11755 Doc No. C06550458 Date: 05/31/2018\n\n                                      M-2017-11755    B-00001350811      \"UNCLASSIFIED\"       7/10/2026\n\n\n\n\n      PAGE 06    STATE 230684 152118Z\n      DISCUSSION GOES ON \"NAMING NAMES.\" WITH CHANGES IN\n       SLOVAKIA AND BULGARIA, WE RUN THE RISK OF HAVING TO NAME\n      EVERYBODY.                                      THE                      25X6\n      SECRETARY CONTINUED THAT WE NEED A CREDIBLE OPEN DOOR                                                                           25X9      PACKAGE, NOT PFP-PLUS BUT RATHER A MEMBERSHIP ACTION PLAN\n      THAT WOULD STRENGTHEN THE CANDIDATES FOR NATO. THIS GROUP\n      WHICH HAS CHOSEN TO PURSUE MEMBERSHIP MUST BE SET APART\n     FROM THE OTHER PARTNERS. WE CANNOT JUST PROVIDE THEM A\n       \"WAITING ROOM.\"\n\n         10.                                                                   25X6\n                                                                           25X9\n\n\n\n\n       \"NO FIRST USE\" IS NOT A U.S.-ONLY ISSUE\n\n         11. (C) THE SECRETARY EXPRESSED CONCERN WITH\\                                                                           25X6               /GERMAN PLANS REGARDING \"NO FIRST USE.\" SHE HAD\n                                                                           25X9      RECEIVED ASSURANCES FROM CANADA AND GERMANY THAT IT WOULD\n      NOT BE RAISED, AT LEAST NOT AT THE PLENARY.    I\n\n\n\n                                       I i HE SECRETARY WARNED THAT THE \"NO FIRST USE\"\n       ISSUE HAD WIDER IMPLICATIONS FOR THE ALLIANCE, AND COULD\n      UNRAVEL NATO'S NUCLEAR DOCTRINE. NOW WAS NOT THE TIME FOR\n                 CONFIDENTIAL\n\n      PAGE 07    STATE 230684 152118Z\n       THIS ISSUE TO BE RAISED. AMBASSADOR VERSHBOW NOTED THAT IS\n\n     WAS ABSURD TO SUGGEST THAT INDIA AND PAKISTAN WOULD NOT\n      HAVE TESTED THEIR RESPECTIVE NUCLEAR DEVICES IF NATO HAD A\n       \"NO FIRST USE\" POLICY. NSC SENIOR DIRECTOR BANDLER ALSO\n     WARNED THAT GERMAN DEFENSE MINISTER SCHARPING' S RECENT\n      WASHINGTON VISIT RECEIVED SENATEE2ALTENTION THAT COULD LEAD\n      TO LARGER PROBLEMS ON THE ISSU                                           25X6\n                                                                           25X9            THE SECRETARY NOTED THAT UK PRIME M N STER BLAIR\n      COULD ALSO BE HELPFUL WITH SCHROEDER.\n\n      EUROPEAN DEFENSE\n\n         12. (C) THE SECRETARY NOTED THAT SHE WOULD RAISE ESDI AT\n      THE BREAKFAST WITH KEY ALLIES. GROSSMAN ADDED THAT IT\n     WOULD BE GOOD IF UK FOREIGN MINISTER COOK AND FRENCH\n      FOREIGN MINISTER VEDRINE WERE TO REPORT AT THE NAC PLENARY\n     ON WHAT THEY HAD TOLD THE EU GENERAL AFFAIRS COUNCIL. THE\n      SECRETARY NOTED THAT ESDI, HOWEVER IT EVOLVES, MUST OPERATE\n       WITHIN THE CONTEXT THE ALLIANCE.                                            25X6\n                                                                            25X9\n\n\n\nUNCLASSIFIED U.S. Department of State Case No. M-2017-11755 Doc No. C06550458 Date: 05/31/2018"
        },
        {
          "page": 5,
          "text": "UNCLASSIFIED U.S. Department of State Case No. M-2017-11755 Doc No. C06550458 Date: 05/31/2018\n\n                                      M-2017-11755    B-00001350811      \"UNCLASSIFIED\"       7/10/2026\n\n\n\n                                                                           25X6\n                                                                           25X9\n\n       RUSSIAN/PJC\n\n         13. (C) THE SECRETARY EXPRESSED CONCERN THAT NEITHER\n       VEDRINE, FISCHER NOR ITALIAN FOREIGN MINISTER DINI WERE\n      PLANNING ON ATTENDING THE PJC SESSION. THE SECRETARY NOTED\n                 CONFIDENTIAL\n\n      PAGE 08   STATE 230684 152118Z\n      THAT SHE WOULD RAISE THIS AS AN ISSUE/                                                                           25X6\n                                                                           25X9                                  THE SECRETARY POINTED OUT\n      THE PROBLEMS WERE NOT RESOLVED IN KOSOVO AND THAT THERE\n     WERE TOO MANY MUPNJ FORCES STILL IN PLACE. THOUGH THE KLA\n     WERE NOT ANGELS, WE NEEDED TO KEEP THE PRESSURE ON\n       MILOSEVIC. THE SUCCESS OF KOSOVO WAS THAT OF DIPLOMACY\n      BACKED BY FORCE.\n\n                                                                            25X6\n                                                                            25X9\n\n                  GROSSMAN NOTED THAT THE OSCE HAD HANDLED\n      THE CFE ISSUE WELL AT OSLO. AMBASSADOR VERSHBOW POINTED\n\n      OUT THAT IF RUSSIA WERE WILLING TO NEGOTIATE MORE SERIOUSLY\n        IN VIENNA, THEN THERE COULD FASTER PROGRESS ON THE\n       NEGOTIATIONS.\n       PICKERING\n\n                 CONFIDENTIAL\n\n          &ItAlt; END OF DOCUMENT &gt;&gt;\n\n\n\n\n\nUNCLASSIFIED U.S. Department of State Case No. M-2017-11755 Doc No. C06550458 Date: 05/31/2018"
        }
